-- Source: shadowcore SL-era SQL dumps (same priority/merge rules as 05_creature_templates.sql;
-- all 259 entries had a real source row from the base dump, nothing defaulted this pass).
--
-- displayId NEVER comes from the source dump's own column -- it is always resolved from
-- nath_all_go_display.txt (entry -> retail displayId) and then remapped where that retail
-- id collided with a stock 3.3.5 display:
--   * the 18 named doors (GO_* constants in castle_nathria.h's enum Gameobjects) resolve to
--     the already-deployed batch-1 ids 101186-101194 -- matched by FileDataID (via the
--     community listfile) between each door's retail displayId and the 9 door models
--     already baked into GameObjectDisplayInfo.csv at those ids, NOT by guesswork.
--   * batch-2 (37 models, see GO_DISPLAY_REMAP_NOTE.txt): 33 remapped to 4595008-4595040,
--     4 left as-is (10403, 13594, 39107, 42973 were free).
